prs.body:
Fixes #28128

`array-callback-return` only checked array method calls with exactly one argument, so a callback followed by anything else was skipped. That's why `reduce`/`reduceRight` with an initial value were never reported. The same thing happened to `foo.map(cb, thisArg)` and `Array.from(x, cb, thisArg)`.

ESLint's rule checks the first argument (the second for `Array.from`/`Array.fromAsync`) no matter how many arguments follow it. This PR does the same.

```js
[1, 2].reduce((total, x) => {
  if (x > 1) {
    return total + x;
  }
}, 0); // now reported, same as ESLint
```

Tests: new pass/fail cases for `reduce`/`reduceRight` with an initial value, `map` with `thisArg`, `Array.from` with `thisArg`, and a callback that isn't the first argument (`foo.reduce(bar, function() {})` stays unreported). Snapshot updated. `cargo test -p oxc_linter`, `cargo clippy -p oxc_linter --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check` pass.

AI disclosure: I used an AI assistant while writing this change. I reviewed the code and tests myself.
